-- title:
--   Unit reduced norms of Eichler orders at discriminant 2
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $2$ in the sense of the project predicate: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $2\in v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $N\in\mathbb N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal among orders containing them) with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$, as additive subgroups, equal to $N$. Let $\varepsilon=(\varepsilon_w)_w$ be a family with $\varepsilon_w\in\mathbb Q_w$ and $v(\varepsilon_w)=1$ for every height-one prime $w$. Then there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ lying in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26), the stabiliser for the multiplicative action on the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral, such that for every $w$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{I},z_{J},z_{K})$ for all $z$ and $r$, the reduced norm $x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_I^2-bx_J^2+ab\,x_K^2$ of $\varphi$ applied to the $w$-component of $u$ equals $\varepsilon_w$.
--
--   This is the idelic form of the local surjectivity of the reduced norm on an Eichler order, $\mathrm{nrd}(R_w^\times)=\mathbb Z_w^\times$ at every finite place, in the case where the quaternion algebra is definite and ramified exactly at the finite place $2$; the case of odd ramification is treated separately, and the two are combined in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_forall_nrd_eq_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_forall_nrd_eq_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt). It feeds the strong approximation arguments used in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_ne`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_ne) and [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_units_forall_mem_iff_mem_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_units_forall_mem_iff_mem_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem).
